NAME
     vhold - hold vector state for a while

SYNOPSIS
     vhold [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
     vhold touches the vector registers every 10 ms for SECONDS, so that
     at any instant a host asking whether a task holds state in the unit
     gets a deterministic yes. It exits 0 when the time is up and prints
     the sum it computed, so the registers were really used. The
     negotiation tests use it to make a refusal certain.

SEE ALSO
     vecprobe(1), memck(1)
